§§ DESIGN-PILLARS
  a Thompson-NFA ← no-backtracking • O(mn) worst-case guaranteed
  b RE2-style ← linear-time • predictable performance
  c Unicode-aware ← CSLv3 is glyph-heavy ∴ UTF-8 support mandatory
  d subset-grammar ← skip PCRE-only features • keep-essentials
  e deterministic-output ← same-regex same-input → same-match bytes
  f streaming-compat ← operate on-byte-stream ¬ only-full-string
  g self-contained ← zero-external-deps • all-Odin
  h selftest-disciplined ← ≥ 30 test-vectors across feature-matrix

§§ FEATURE MATRIX (recommended-subset)
  REGEX-FEATURES :
    ✓ literals : any-UTF-8 byte-sequence
    ✓ escape : \n \t \r \\ \. \* \+ \? \( \) \[ \] \{ \} \| \^ \$
    ✓ character-classes : [abc] [^abc] [a-z] [0-9]
    ✓ predefined-classes : \d \D \s \S \w \W \.
    ✓ Unicode-classes : \p{L} \p{N} \p{P} (letter / number / punct)
    ✓ quantifiers : * + ? {n} {n,} {n,m}
    ✓ greedy + lazy : *? +? ?? {n,m}?
    ✓ anchors : ^ $ \b \B
    ✓ alternation : a|b
    ✓ grouping : (expr) + (?:expr) non-capturing
    ✓ capture-groups : numbered + named (?<name>expr)
    ✓ backreferences to-captures : \1 \2 \k<name>
    ◐ lookahead : (?=expr) (?!expr)     ← maybe-defer to-v1.4.1
    ◐ lookbehind : (?<=expr) (?<!expr)  ← maybe-defer to-v1.4.1
  NOT-SUPPORTED (intentional) :
    N! PCRE-recursion
    N! atomic-groups (?>expr)
    N! conditional-patterns (?(1)yes|no)
    N! possessive-quantifiers *+ ++ ?+
  ∵ lookahead/lookbehind break pure-NFA guarantee
  ∵ defer-decision : attempt in-extra-pass if-time OR defer to-v1.4.1

§§ ARCHITECTURE
  parser/regex.odin                  ~400 LOC  public-API + orchestration
    types : Regex • Match • Group
    compile(pattern : string) → (Regex, Err)
    match(re : Regex, input : string) → Match
    find_all(re : Regex, input : string) → []Match
    replace(re : Regex, input : string, template : string) → string
    free(re : Regex)
  parser/regex_parse.odin            ~500 LOC  pattern-parser
    tokenize pattern → AST (Alt / Concat / Repeat / Class / Anchor / ...)
    char-class resolver (ranges + predefined + Unicode)
    error-recovery + position-tracking
  parser/regex_compile.odin          ~400 LOC  AST → NFA
    Thompson-construction
    state-table + transition-table
    epsilon-closure precomputation
  parser/regex_nfa.odin              ~300 LOC  NFA simulation-core
    VM-style execution
    work-list BFS ← linear-time guarantee
    capture-group tracking
  parser/regex_unicode.odin          ~600 LOC  Unicode tables
    \p{L} \p{N} \p{P} code-point ranges (subset of UCD)
    UTF-8 encode/decode helpers
    case-folding (for-ASCII only initially)
  tests/test_regex.odin              ~400 LOC  selftest
    ≥ 30 vectors : literal + class + anchor + quant + capture + alt

§§ SELFTEST VECTORS (target ≥ 30)
  literal :
    "abc" matches "abc"              → full
    "abc" matches "xabcy"            → partial
    "abc" does-not-match "aXc"       → no-match
  escape :
    "\\." matches "."                → literal-dot
    "a\\|b" matches "a|b"            → pipe-escape
  character-class :
    "[a-z]" matches "x"
    "[^0-9]" matches "a"
    "\\d" matches "5"
    "\\w" matches "foo_1"
  Unicode :
    "\\p{L}" matches "§"  (well ← § not-letter) ∴ adjust
    "\\p{L}" matches "中"  → letter-category
    "\\p{N}" matches "5"
  quantifier :
    "a*" matches ""
    "a*" matches "aaaa"
    "a+" does-not-match ""
    "a{3}" matches "aaa"
    "a{2,4}" matches "aaa"
    "a{2,4}" does-not-match "a"
  lazy :
    "a+?" on "aaaa" captures "a" (shortest)
    "a+"  on "aaaa" captures "aaaa" (longest)
  anchors :
    "^abc" matches "abcde"
    "^abc" does-not-match "xabc"
    "abc$" matches "xabc"
    "\\babc" matches "abc def"
  alternation :
    "cat|dog" matches "cat"
    "cat|dog" matches "dog"
    "cat|dog" does-not-match "bird"
  grouping + capture :
    "(abc)" captures "abc" at-group-1
    "(?:abc)" does-not-capture
    "(?<name>abc)" captures at-group-name
    "(a)(b)(c)" captures 3 groups
  backreferences :
    "(.)\\1" matches "aa"
    "(.)\\1" does-not-match "ab"
  find-all :
    "\\d+" on "a1b22c333" finds [1, 22, 333]
  replace :
    replace "a+" with "X" on "aaabaaa" → "XbX"
    backref : replace "(\\w+)" with "<$1>" on "foo" → "<foo>"
  Apocky-specific :
    "'[dfsmtepgr]" matches "'d"       ← CSLv3 morpheme
    "§+" matches "§§§"                ← CSLv3 section-nesting
    "[⊑⊗→]" matches "⊗"               ← CSLv3 operator-class

§§ CLI-SURFACE (additive only)
  parser.exe --regex-match <pattern> <input>      → 0=match 1=no-match
  parser.exe --regex-find <pattern> <input>       → emit match-spans JSON
  parser.exe --regex-replace <pat> <repl> <input> → emit replaced-string
  parser.exe --regex-selftest                     → run selftest-suite
  parser.exe --regex-compile-check <pattern>      → syntax-validate

