═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
§ THEORETICAL-NOTES ← §§ A8-depth-hints
═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  Thompson-NFA :
    1968 paper ← Ken Thompson "Regular Expression Search Algorithm"
    construction : per-operator NFA-fragment + compose
    characters : single-state match
    alternation : fork-states
    concat : serial
    repeat : loop-states
    classic-reference : Cox "Regular Expression Matching Can Be Simple and Fast"
  NFA vs DFA :
    NFA : O(mn) worst-case • simpler construction • lower-memory
    DFA : O(n) matching • exponential-state worst-case • higher-memory
    recommend NFA ∵ predictable-worst-case + simpler
    optional : DFA-cache for-hot-patterns (v1.5+ optimization)
  Thompson-construction :
    1 parse pattern → AST
    2 recursive descent AST → NFA-fragment (in + out state-pointers)
    3 concat : wire-out of-left to-in of-right
    4 alt : new-start with-epsilon to-both + new-end
    5 star : new-start with-epsilon to-in AND to-new-end (+ loop)
  Pike-VM alternative :
    instead-of NFA-states : bytecode-VM
    instructions : CHAR • MATCH • JMP • SPLIT • SAVE
    simpler-impl + easy to-add features
    RE2 uses this approach
    M? consider ← ~same LOC • different abstraction
    recommend Pike-VM ∵ feature-extensibility future-proofing
  Unicode strategy :
    full UCD : ~30MB data
    subset : L + N + P + S + Z + C = ~5MB encoded-as-ranges
    CSLv3-needs : L (letters incl-Greek) + N + P + S (symbols)
    trap : UTF-8 decode per-codepoint vs per-byte scanning
    recommend per-rune NFA • byte-level for-ASCII-only fast-path
  Backreferences :
    breaks NFA-purity ← requires-backtracking OR linear-time-requires-Aho-Corasick-extension
    simple-impl : limit-to-anchored + emit-warning for-general-case
    alt-impl : separate post-match check-pass
    M? defer to-v1.4.1 if-timing-tight
  JSON-Schema pattern :
    ECMAScript-regex subset ← our-A8 supports-superset
    wire-up : compile-pattern-at-schema-parse + match-on-validate
    cache : reuse compiled-Regex across-validate-calls
    trap : JSON-Schema allows invalid-regex patterns ← must-error-gracefully

